Cell["\<\
So as we can see our estimate of the Wiener system static nonlinearity, n2(\
\[CenterDot]),  is very close to the actual static nonlinear element, n(\
\[CenterDot]), over the middle region of its range but on either side of this \
the fit is not good. This is typical of polynomial fits where the fit is good \
where there are plenty of data points (in the middle here) but degrades at \
the extremes.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.783719290990895*^9, 3.7837193991868715`*^9}, {
   3.783950954000724*^9, 3.783950954109677*^9}, {3.783986735042588*^9, 
   3.783986735136224*^9}, 3.784032340413211*^9, {3.784131346389725*^9, 
   3.7841314473929586`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"1c66adb4-a90b-4679-80e0-\
032e511f00b0"],

Cell["\<\
Now that we have the new estimate, n2(\[CenterDot]), we can predict the \
output, y2(t), from our u3(t) estimate:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.783767802005376*^9, 3.783767885369144*^9}, {
  3.7839867765582356`*^9, 
  3.78398678676464*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"d6b9acc4-efea-4ac0-8a42-\
62351603c3b2"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  ButtonBox["\<\"\[GraySquare]\"\>",
   Appearance->"Frameless",
