Cell["\<\
This discovery function returns static models together with a \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Score\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] and a measure of \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]Complexity\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote]. A \
\[OpenCurlyDoubleQuote]good\[CloseCurlyDoubleQuote] model is one which has a \
high Score (a good fit) but a low level of complexity under the assumption \
that simplicity is important. Most of the functions returned by FindFormula[ \
] are way too complex and unfortunately the FindFormula[ ] function does not \
by default test for the LogisticSigmoid[ ] function. So lets assume that by \
looking at n2 we decided to try a LogisticSigmoid function then we could use \
our trusty Levenberg-Marquardt nonlinear minimization technique to fit this \
function to our data:\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.7840551170974817`*^9, 3.784055361486759*^9}, {
  3.784055440114767*^9, 3.78405552007748*^9}, {3.784055571865853*^9, 
  3.784055627242165*^9}, {3.784055660406129*^9, 3.7840556812183466`*^9}, {
  3.784055752246482*^9, 3.784055810822974*^9}, {3.784124263833822*^9, 
  3.784124338556278*^9}, {3.784124499600365*^9, 
  3.784124657501763*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"9a892cd1-7f92-4056-84ca-\
1d28f1f02a4f"],

